<div class="text guide-styles" data-units-dynamic="article" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">
<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Shadow Priest DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Shadow Priest DPS Phase 4</h2>One of your primary goals is to get your hands on 4-Piece of <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=1067/regalia-of-dying-light">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of Dying Light</span></a>. If you have 4-Piece of <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-359/regalia-of-the-cleansing-flame">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of the Cleansing Flame</span></a> from Heroic Firelands, you will likely not see much benefit until you obtain at least the Normal version of <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=1067/regalia-of-dying-light">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of Dying Light</span></a>. You will however be able to practice your new rotation and you gain a Burst Window which can be useful for fights like Spine of Deathwing. It is important to note that with the shift from <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-359/regalia-of-the-cleansing-flame">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of the Cleansing Flame</span></a>, your rotation will change as well as soon as you get your hands on a full set of Tier 13. You can find more details in our rotation guide.<br/>
<br/>With how homogenous stats have become in Cataclysm and our ability to utilize all stats to some extent, gearing is not nearly as rigid as it once was, and you can for the most part get away with using less ideal pieces without taking a massive hit. This is especially true if you <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/item-reforging-overview">Reforge</a> effectively. We want to highlight that with <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=1067/regalia-of-dying-light">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of Dying Light</span></a>, your Reforging priorities will change. We would recommend checking out the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/priest/shadow/dps-stat-priority-attributes-pve">Stat Priority</a> guide for more information on this. Additionally, with Intellect being the biggest DPS gain, a higher item level piece will almost always be the better choice.<br/>
<br/>The main exceptions will consistently be your Trinkets, as their value primarily comes from their unique effects. I always recommend simming Trinkets before making a decision, as your Trinket combo, fight length, group composition, and any number of other variables can and will impact what is the best choice for you at any given time.<div class="pad"></div>
