<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">Valor Points for Shadow Priest DPS Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> are Cataclysm's version of Raid Emblems, which means that they can be obtained by killing bosses in Raids and completing Heroic Dungeons through the Random Dungeon Finder tool. The main vendors you can exchange these at to obtain gear are <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=46556/jamusvaz">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Jamus'Vaz</span></a> for the Horde and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=44245/faldren-tillsdale">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Faldren Tillsdale</span></a> for the Alliance.<br/>
<br/> There is a weekly cap of 1600 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>, meaning any purchase using this currency will take multiple weeks to complete. This cap carries over week to week, so you won't be falling behind on <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> if you missed the cap for one week. <br/>
<br/>There are no Tier Pieces from <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> this time around. Of the items listed below, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77098/nanoprecise-cape">
<img alt="Nanoprecise Cape" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_deathwingraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nanoprecise Cape</span></a> will be something you keep for your best in slot. There are items listed below that are also good until you start replacing them in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a>, as they will be better than some of the gear you picked up during <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5723/firelands">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Firelands</span></a>. I'd also recommend taking a look at your auction house to see if pieces like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77177/splinterfoot-sandals">
<img alt="Splinterfoot Sandals" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_robe_raidpriest_k_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Splinterfoot Sandals</span></a> can be picked up for a good price.<br/>
