<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-shadow-priest-dps">Trinkets for Shadow Priest DPS</h4>Your ideal Trinkets this time around are <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77995/will-of-unbinding">
<img alt="Will of Unbinding" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_stonetablet_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Will of Unbinding</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78000/cunning-of-the-cruel">
<img alt="Cunning of the Cruel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_coin_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cunning of the Cruel</span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77991/insignia-of-the-corrupted-mind">
<img alt="Insignia of the Corrupted Mind" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bijou_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Insignia of the Corrupted Mind</span></a> isn't the worst pick up if you are missing <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69110/variable-pulse-lightning-capacitor">
<img alt="Variable Pulse Lightning Capacitor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_naxxramas06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Variable Pulse Lightning Capacitor</span></a>, however it is weaker than the other options since we don't want to cast faster than Shadowfiend attacks when wearing <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=1067/regalia-of-dying-light">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of Dying Light</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>There is also some niche value in picking up Trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=72898/foul-gift-of-the-demon-lord">
<img alt="Foul Gift of the Demon Lord" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_felflamering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Foul Gift of the Demon Lord</span></a>. You can equip and activate it just before a fight, and then swap to something better before the fight starts. Keep in mind that this carries some risks with it not proccing in time for the pull.<br/>
<br/>It is also worth shouting out <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77114/bottled-wishes">
<img alt="Bottled Wishes" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_109.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bottled Wishes</span></a> from Valor Points as a very competitive option before your main Trinkets.<br/>
<br/>Remember, Trinkets are very, very dependent on fights. Every variable in a fight, including your gear, group, fight length, mechanics, etc, will change the value of Trinkets. I recommend always simming Trinkets to find out the best for you instead of purely relying on a list.<div class="pad"></div>
